WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.350
In 1980, Bangladesh's total fertility
rate was 6.3 births per woman.

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.290
By 2024, it had fallen to 2.1.

3
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.790
A rate of 2.1 is called replacement level.

4
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:20.010
In Niger, over the same years, the
rate fell only from 7.8 to 5.9.

5
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.310
Was it a law?

6
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.490
Fewer marriages?

7
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:26.390
What changed for women in Bangladesh
to shrink families so fast?

8
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:31.430
In this mission, you'll test four levers
that can change how many children families

9
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.530
have.

10
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.130
Then you'll compare women's
lives in Bangladesh and Niger,

11
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.770
figure by figure.

12
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.230
Your mission: find out what changed for
women in Bangladesh to shrink families

13
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.590
from about six children to two.
